rogue -- the rogue 5.3 clone============================    rogueThe dungeon is drawn as you explore it: walls and doors, `@' for you,letters for monsters and symbols for what lies on the floor.  The line atthe foot is your dungeon level, gold, hit points, strength, armour andexperience.  Find the stairs down (`>') and go deeper.h, j, k and l move one square; `i' lists what you carry (SPACE puts thelist away); `d' drops something.  ESC cancels a question.  `Q' and then`y' end the game and show the Top Ten, kept in GAMES/ROGUE/rogue.scores.It needs TERM set, as SYS/login does.Tim Stoehr's clone of rogue 5.3, as comp.sources.games posted it with itsthree patches.  Full originals in SRC/rogue/ORIG.